From: price@price.demon.co.uk (Michael Clive Price)
Date: Sat, 12 Feb 94 22:58:30 GMT
Subject: [#94-2-120] PCR

Recently I've been chatting with an atheist friend suffering cognitive
disssonance from a Catholic upbringing.  He is, consequently, obsessed
with trying to justify all his new beliefs, tastes, etc and running into
infinite regress.  (Is this a common problem with people that lose an
all-encompassing prescriptive religion?  They're looking for some other
single system with "all the answers"?)  He is receiving therapy, trying
to put himself back together.  If ever anyone was more in need of PCR! 
So, I thought I'd try explaining PCR to him - how he didn't have to
justify all his beliefs, it was sufficient to be open to criticism
(which he already is) etc.  He was greatly impressed, more so than I
expected, and opined that the (brief) explanation I gave was probably
worth a year's therapy!

I may try it on some other people as well.

